  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607197600: PostgreSQL version matrix and bounded contention soak

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

PostgreSQL qualification requires majors 14, 15 and 17 on JDK 21 or newer.
JDK 11 is not a supported cell: all three attempted cells fail before runtime
with the absent `javax.crypto.KEM` class used by secret authority. The matrix,
features, soak terminal invariants and commands are owned by the machine-readable
`docs/postgresql-qualification.edn` contract. Linux x86_64 runs the same three
released versions as a required non-fail-fast CI matrix.

The interop gate also runs three guest consumer instances through two physical
pool connections for 90 acquire/query/reset/release operations. Guest query
scratch is reused at fixed bounded addresses rather than growing linear memory.
Completion requires no leases, waiters or native handles.

## Evidence

The full crash, half-open, rotation, pool and protocol qualification passes on
Homebrew PostgreSQL 14.19, 15.13 and 17.9 with Temurin 21 on macOS arm64. The
contention soak completes 30 operations from each of three concurrent workers,
retains exactly two physical connections until close, and terminates cleanly.

This closes the locally available released-version matrix and bounded
contention soak. Linux CI results and longer wall-clock soak remain freshness
evidence, not permission to weaken the contract.")))
